<article class="env-example" id="0CDL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CDL">Example <span data-tag="0CDL">55.15.1</span>.</a> Let $R = \mathbf{R}[[\pi ]]$ and consider the scheme </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  X = V(T_1^2 + T_2^2 - \pi T_0^2) \subset \mathbf{P}^2_ R  \]
</div>
  <p> The base change of $X$ to $\mathbf{C}[[\pi ]]$ is isomorphic to the scheme defined in Example <a href="/tag/0CA0" data-tag="0CA0">55.10.3</a> because we have the factorization $T_1^2 + T_2^2 = (T_1 + iT_2)(T_1 - iT_2)$ over $\mathbf{C}$. Thus $X$ is regular and its special fibre is irreducible yet singular, hence $X$ is the unique minimal model of its generic fibre (use Lemma <a href="/tag/0CDA" data-tag="0CDA">55.12.4</a>). It follows that an extension is needed even in genus $0$. </p>
</article>